#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#In most instances the vehicle sprung mass is measured at design load, meaning that driver, passenger, and fuel are not included in the measurements. If that is not the case, or if a different passenger or fuel loading condition needs to be tested, here is an example demonstrating how to set this up.
#
#In this example, a vehicle has payloads added for both a driver and a half tank of fuel.  Click on the Vehicle: Loaded Condition dataset called "B-Class, Sports Car w/ Driver and Fuel" to see how this was set up.
#
#Payloads are added to vehicles on the Vehicle: Loaded Condition screen. Use the gray Library drop-down arrow above the vehicle blue link to select this option. You may also browse to the Vehicle: Loaded Condition library directly using the Libraries drop-down menu at the top of this screen and selecting Vehicles => Vehicle: Loaded Condition.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

